---
layout: layouts/page.njk
---
{#- An infobox that carries only its own "See also" row is furniture: it says
    nothing about the nation, floats a framed panel into the first paragraph, and
    on a phone pushes the prose a screen down to do it. Three nations are in that
    position — the Principalities of the Reach, Rues and T'barris — and it is not
    an oversight to fill in later: source-material/markdown records that the book
    names no capital and no demonym for any of them, and for the Principalities
    says outright that there is no single capital and no shared name for the
    people. Those three pages get no infobox. The "All nations" link is in the
    sidebar on every one of them. -#}
{% if capital or demonym %}
<aside class="infobox" style="--nation-color: {{ color }}">
  <p class="infobox__flag" aria-hidden="true"></p>
  {% include "partials/ornaments/divider.njk" %}
  <dl>
    {% if capital %}<dt>Capital</dt><dd>{{ capital }}</dd>{% endif %}
    {% if demonym %}<dt>Demonym</dt><dd>{{ demonym }}</dd>{% endif %}
    <dt>See also</dt><dd><a href="/lore/nations/">All nations</a></dd>
  </dl>
</aside>
{% endif %}
<p class="lede">{{ summary }}</p>
{{ content | safe }}
